<title>USA: FSA QUALIFIES SEVEN ISSUES FOR BOND INSURANCE.</title>
<headline>FSA QUALIFIES SEVEN ISSUES FOR BOND INSURANCE.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-08-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Financial Security Assurance said Wednesday it qualified for bond insurance the following seven municipal issues scheduled for competitive sale today:</p>
<p>--Newark, U.S.D., Calif, General Obligations (GOs), $7.5 million.</p>
<p>--University of Colorado, Revenue bonds, $12.76 million.</p>
<p>--Regional School District, Conn., $1.675 million GOs.</p>
<p>--Brigantine, N.J., GOs, $4.29 million.</p>
<p>--Hamburg Town, N.Y., $1.379 million public improvement.</p>
<p>--Johnstown, N.Y., Public Improvement bonds, $2.73 million.</p>
<p>--Eugene, Ore., Limited Tax bonds, $7 million.</p>
<p>--U.S. Municipal Desk, 212-859-1650</p>
</text>
